{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/workroom implementation at exact clean pushed head 914e39641b034b76234cce1f4aaf5e624f938607 on request/dated-active-cause-v2, rebased onto main 9ec7109c, fulfilling planner's 2906cb7e under promise 60bdd5ee. It answers codex's changes-requested at 01c8277e, which I ratified at 1b385992, and it is the fifth head on this lane.\n\nEVERY POSITION-SENSITIVE FACT NOW LIVES INSIDE THE POSITIONED SCOPE. Two of codex's four findings were the same mistake in two places. A StalenessTerminal basis catches staleness without passing it on, and that has to govern the date as well as the flag: inheriting a cause the basis stopped dated a candidate before a verdict that stalenessAsOf holds was signed over an unmoved world. And the successor topology was taken from the fold rather than the scope, so a supersession that landed after a verdict could reach back, condemn the merge plan at that verdict and revoke receipt authority the reviewer's signature had already earned. Both are now scoped by asOf, and succeededRetirements is the scope's own method.\n\nTHE TWO REGRESSIONS ARE DETERMINISTIC. Codex found both by randomized differential and said targeted tests did not cover them, which was true. The Terminal case is now pinned by a log where the verdict sits strictly between the stopped cause and the basis's own retirement, so the two candidate dates are distinguishable rather than coincidentally equal. The successor case proves non-vacuity first -- the end-of-log projection does condemn -- so position is the only variable left when the receipt is admitted.\n\nGATES I RAN AT THIS EXACT HEAD, not taken from the implementing agent's report: gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... green across every package; go test -race -count=1 on internal/workroom and internal/app clean; GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... clean; git diff --check clean; worktree clean; origin equals the head.\n\nMUTATIONS I RAN MYSELF, restoring and confirming a clean tree after each. Removing 'mode != StalenessTerminal' from the inheritance guard kills TestADirectlyRetiredTerminalBasisDoesNotDateByTheCauseItStopped with 'candidate dated 16, want 19, the terminal basis's own retirement'. Changing the call site in validateMergeReceiptNow from scope.succeededRetirements() to f.succeededRetirements() kills TestASuccessionDeclaredAfterTheVerdictDoesNotCondemnThePlanAtIt with the plan condemned and receipt authority revoked. Deleting the 'record.sequence() \u003e s.asOf' filter inside the scope's own topology kills the same test the same way, which is the point: the guard and the call site are one fact, and either half alone is not enough.","body":{"commit":"914e39641b034b76234cce1f4aaf5e624f938607","path":"internal/workroom"}}